  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Before becoming a yacht restorer, Bill Bolling had been a competitive swimmer, Hollywood stunt performer and advertising executive. He graduated from Northwestern University and worked in his father’s agency, including responsibility for its Los Angeles office. A move to Fort Lauderdale brought him into yacht deliveries and refurbishment.\n\nWriting gave Bolling another outlet for his experience on the water. From a home in Marathon, Florida, he and Patsy contributed a powerboat column to TheYACHT magazine. After retiring to New Smyrna Beach, he created an adventure trail with hidden mechanical surprises, incorporating objects donated by friends, including a small locomotive and a glider.",
    "html": "<p>Before becoming a yacht restorer, Bill Bolling had been a competitive swimmer, Hollywood stunt performer and advertising executive. He graduated from Northwestern University and worked in his father’s agency, including responsibility for its Los Angeles office. A move to Fort Lauderdale brought him into yacht deliveries and refurbishment.</p>\r\n<p>Writing gave Bolling another outlet for his experience on the water. From a home in Marathon, Florida, he and Patsy contributed a powerboat column to TheYACHT magazine. After retiring to New Smyrna Beach, he created an adventure trail with hidden mechanical surprises, incorporating objects donated by friends, including a small locomotive and a glider.</p>\r\n",
